androidx.games:games-text-input:3.0.1
Source: https://dl.google.com/android/maven2/androidx/games/games-text-input/3.0.1/games-text-input-3.0.1.aar
Fetched: 2026-08-04

Vendored per ../../PLAN.md §5 (IME) and phase_0/README.md's original finding:
"GameTextInput is standalone-usable ... the C++ file is small enough to fold
into the existing cc-crate/NDK cross-compile in build.rs." That's exactly what
../build.rs does with include/game-text-input/gametextinput.cpp below.

What's here, straight from the AAR's own prefab layout (paths preserved so a
diff against a future AAR version is trivial):
  include/game-text-input/gametextinput.{h,cpp}  the C API + its implementation
  include/game-text-input/gamecommon.h            small shared macros
  include/common/gamesdk_common.h                 version-packing macro
  classes.jar                                     compiled Java classes (InputConnection,
                                                    GameTextInput, Listener, Settings, State) —
                                                    used as-is (javac classpath + merged into
                                                    the app's classes.dex via d8), not recompiled
                                                    from source, since only the prebuilt AAR ships
                                                    class files, not .java sources.

Deliberately NOT vendored: the prebuilt static libs under prefab/modules/*/libs/
(one .a per ABI) — see ../build.rs's own comment on why compiling
gametextinput.cpp ourselves (instead of linking those) was the simpler, more
consistent-with-the-rest-of-this-repo choice.

